  "description": "Bridgeport ST is one of Haro's most popular commuters and features a Solum Series hybrid frame that features Rider Optimized Geometry specifically designed to assure a proper and comfortable fit. Most importantly, Bridgeport ST features a gender neutral step-thru designed frame that makes it easier to dismount when swinging a leg around the rear wheel is not desirable or not possible. The word Solum refers to the upper layer of a soil profile, which means that in addition to its on asphalt commuting skills it can also venture out onto that upper layer of soil that presents itself as unpaved lake and fire roads. Bridgeport ST is versatile and features a Suntour NEX HLO suspension fork with just the right amount of travel for a bike like this. The suspension fork absorbs small bumps off road, and when you ride on road it has a hydraulic lockout that allows you to make the fork rigid which maximizes the energy from your pedaling efforts. Bridgeport ST comes complete with a Shimano 21 speed drive train that includes EZ Fire shifters. Its wheelset is made from Pivit alloy 28h disc hubs laced to 700c alloy double wall rims and all weather stopping is made possible thanks to a pair of Tektro Aries mechanical disc brakes.\nHaro Solum Dual Sport frame with Rider Optimized Geometry, mechanically-shaped alloy tubing, and chainstay disc brake mount\nSR Suntour NEX HLO suspension fork with 63mm travel and hydraulic lockout\nShimano TY-301 crankset, 48/38/28 and sealed cartridge BB\nShimano Altus rear derailleur\nShimano Tourney 7 speed EZ Fire shifters, front derailleur\nPivit disc brake hubs and lightweight double wall rims\nNew Pivit alloy 9* sweep riser bar, and forged stem\nTektro Aires mechanical disc brakes",
